# Shell scripts must keep LF endings even on Windows checkouts. The
# PreToolUse git guardrail (.claude/hooks/block-dangerous-git.sh) runs under
# bash; with CRLF endings it fails to execute, and because that hook fails
# CLOSED a broken hook blocks every Bash command rather than none — which
# would silently kill the unattended overnight runner.
*.sh text eol=lf
